// HARD SUN CONTACT SHADOWS — the pixel side (PHOTON P5, RY-R3; lane
// PHOTON-RAYS-1; SPECS/photon/C4_RAYS_BEYOND_REFLECTIONS_DESIGN.md section 1).
//
// CAUTION for editors: the Hlms parser executes an at-directive even inside a
// comment (DOCS/traps/ENGINE.md). Never write one in this file's comments.
//
// WHAT IT DOES. The ray tier traced one hardware ray per pixel (or per 2x2
// block) from the surface the prepass drew towards the sun, out to the contact
// range, and wrote jahSunVis: 1 where nothing was in the way, 0 where
// something was (rq_sun_contact.comp). Here that answer is folded into the
// FIRST directional light's shadow term — the sun's, the one the shadow map
// was rendered for — as
//
//     fShadow = min( fShadow, jahSunVis )
//
// so the map keeps every shadow it has (the ray can only darken) and the ray
// closes the band of light the map's depth bias leaves at a contact. Beyond
// the range the ray answers 1 and the map is alone, unchanged.
//
// WHY THIS PIECE AND NOT custom_ps_preLights. The material graph defines
// custom_ps_preLights per datablock, and a second definition of a piece fails
// the whole shader. The sun's shadow reaches the light loop through ONE piece,
// DarkenWithShadowFirstLight (Pbs/Any/ShadowMapping_piece_ps.any, inserted as
// the first caster directional's factor in 800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any's
// DoDirectionalLights), and that is the piece the cloud layer's ground shadow
// already redefines (JahFog_piece_vs_piece_ps.any, CLOUDS-2D-1). This library
// folder's files are parsed in sorted order, so this file comes after the fog
// file and its redefinition wins; it COMPOSES with the cloud's instead of
// replacing it — the cloud's factor is the named piece JahCloudSunFactor
// (empty wherever the cloud layer is not in the pass), so the sun's term is
// min( map, ray ) times the sheet's transmittance whichever features are on.
//
// WHERE IT EXISTS, and each term is a reason:
//   jah_sun_contact             the pass claimed the texture (the ray tier
//                               registers it in front of the view's PrePassUse
//                               pass only — never a capture, a probe or a card
//                               pass); its VALUE is the texel divisor
//   hlms_use_prepass            the pass that reads the prepass: fShadow here is
//                               the prepass' own shadow term, and the ray
//                               started from the same prepass' depth
//   hlms_screen_pos_int         iFragCoord is declared
//   hlms_lights_directional     a directional CASTER exists (the sun that casts
//   hlms_num_shadow_map_lights  a map); a sun without one keeps no shadow at all
//   receive_shadows             upstream's own gate on the first light's factor:
//                               a material that receives no shadow receives no
//                               contact shadow either
//   not a caster, not a prepass the two passes that write no colour
//   not alpha-blended           GA-GLASS's rule (GATHER-1b): a Fade or Blend
//                               renderable in the PrePassUse pass is drawn over
//                               an OPAQUE surface's prepass texels, and the
//                               texel under its fragment is that surface's
//                               answer — a floor's contact shadow would be
//                               painted on a glass pane. The pane keeps the map's
//                               term alone. Guarded HERE rather than by
//                               withdrawing the property in the listener: the
//                               slot stays claimed and bound (a dead register
//                               for the pane, as the cloud field's is), and the
//                               rule sits beside the read it protects.
@property( jah_sun_contact && hlms_use_prepass && hlms_screen_pos_int && hlms_lights_directional && hlms_num_shadow_map_lights && receive_shadows && !hlms_alphablend && !hlms_shadowcaster && !hlms_prepass )
	@undefpiece( DarkenWithShadowFirstLight )
	@piece( DarkenWithShadowFirstLight )* ( min( fShadow, midf_c( OGRE_Load2D( jahSunVis, iFragCoord / @value( jah_sun_contact ), 0 ).x ) ) @insertpiece( JahCloudSunFactor ) )@end
@end
